      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": [
        {
          "NlmCategory": "OBJECTIVE",
          "Label": "PURPOSE",
          "content": "To evaluate the efficacy of dextroamphetamine sulfate for idiopathic frozen shoulder in a woman being treated for blad- der urgency and inability to lose weight despite dieting."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "MATERIALS AND METHODS",
          "content": "Dextroamphetamine sulfate was initiated at 15 mg extended release capsules increasing to 25 mg extended release capsules to a 47-year-old woman."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "RESULTS",
          "Label": "RESULTS",
          "content": "She lost 19 pounds in four months, her bladder urgency disappeared, and she had complete resolution of the idiopathic frozen shoulder problem."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "Label": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "content": "Idiopathic frozen shoulder syndrome can be added to the long list of conditions that are related to hypofunction of the sympathetic nervous system and all respond to dextroamphetamine sulfate therapy. They gynecologist is more familial with this syndrome be- cause of it being the main cause of pelvic pain. Thus the gynecologist may become the physician who subsequently treats orthopedic or rheumatological problems or other health issues."
        }
      ]},
